8/1106/1114/1133/1230/1312/1354/1365/1366/1422/1521/1538/1656/1683/1779/1893). Controls: comparable non-crossing window pairs earlier and later show only ordinary turnover (Jaccard 0.50 and 0.48), so 0.0 is far outside background drift; old partners have almost no activity after the switch and new partners almost none before, ruling out mere popularity/degree effects; and group event volume remains substantial across the whole period (only a mild dip in the transition bins), so the discontinuity is not an artefact of missing activity."}, "raw_final_response": "All checks are consistent. Baseline (same-length, non-crossing) window pairs show Jaccard \u2248 0.48\u20130.50, while the pair straddling t\u224839396 shows Jaccard = 0.0 with 138 edges dropped and 97 new edges \u2014 a complete partner replacement, not gradual drift. Old partners are near-absent after the switch and new partners near-absent before, so this isn't a popularity/exposure artifact; group activity continues throughout (no data gap explanation).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_cd75e8ee\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [103, 462, 719, 836, 866, 1224, 1318, 1374, 1415, 1598, 1610, 1826],\n  \"window\": [34396, 44396],\n  \"confidence\": 0.91,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Neighbourhood-turnover series for the group peaks at 1.0 (complete replacement) centred at t=39396, rising sharply from ~0.55-0.60 baseline over roughly 38000-41500 and decaying afterwards. The explicit 5000-unit half-window diff across that point gives Jaccard 0.0: all 138 pre-switch group edges vanish and 97 entirely new ones appear (old cohort 57/234/235/354/511/535/556/559/641/931/1010/1141/1182/1357/1397/1416/1436/1838/1880 -> new cohort 20/156/190/255/324/402/617/728/756/874/929/1088/1106/1114/1133/1230/1312/1354/1365/1366/1422/1521/1538/1656/1683/1779/1893). Controls: comparable non-crossing window pairs earlier and later show only ordinary turnover (Jaccard 0.50 and 0.48), so 0.0 is far outside background drift; old partners have almost no activity after the switch and new partners almost none before, ruling out mere popularity/degree effects; and group event volume remains substantial across the whole period (only a mild dip in the transition bins), so the discontinuity is not an artefact of missing activity.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 33776, "total_output_tokens": 2807, "total_tokens": 36583, "total_latency_ms": 43178, "llm_calls": 5, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}